.TH LUXEDM-SET-DEFAULT 8 "September 2026" "LuxeDM 1.4.1+luxe10"
.SH NAME
luxedm-set-default \- select LuxeDM for the next system boot
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sudo luxedm-set-default
.SH DESCRIPTION
Requests PolicyKit authentication when run by a regular user, records
/usr/bin/luxedm as the selected X11 display manager, and enables the
LuxeDM systemd service through the display-manager.service alias. It does not
stop or replace the display manager serving the current graphical session.
